---
import Ecosystem from "../../components/Ecosystem.astro";
import SnippetBlock from "../../components/SnippetBlock.astro";
import Sheet from "../../layouts/Sheet.astro";
import { itemCounterRows, upstreamCommit } from "../../data/sharedtree-item-counter";

const watershedSource =
  "https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/tree/main/examples/shared_tree_item_counter_lustre";
const fluidSource =
  `https://github.com/microsoft/FluidExamples/tree/${upstreamCommit}/item-counter`;
---

<Sheet
  title="watershed — Fluid SharedTree item-counter, side by side"
  description="The Fluid website's string-array example, rebuilt with native SharedTree and Lustre. Compare real TypeScript and Gleam source for schemas, container setup, subscriptions, and edits."
>
  <header class="comparison-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="back-link"><a href="/sharedtree">Back to the SharedTree comparison</a></p>
      <h1>One array.<br /><em>Two ways to work it.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Insert an entry. Remove the first. Watch the count change in another
        tab. The Fluid website's{" "}
        <a href="https://fluidframework.com/docs/start/examples">simple SharedTree example</a>{" "}
        is small enough to put the whole idea on the table. Here's the same
        behavior in watershed, with the source beside it.
      </p>
      <div class="source-links">
        <a href={watershedSource}>Run the Gleam example</a>
        <a href={fluidSource}>Open the original Fluid example</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="doc-body">
    <div class="g-block introduction">
      <h2>Native tree against native tree.</h2>
      <p>
        Both implementations store an array of strings and display its length.
        Both insert an empty string at the start and leave an empty array alone
        on Remove. The Fluid app uses React; this port uses Lustre. The UI
        frameworks differ, but the shared data and actions don't.
      </p>
      <p>
        This page compares watershed's <strong>native SharedTree API</strong>.
        The <a href="/sharedtree">typed-map comparison</a> follows a different
        design: a graph of channels with a decode boundary. If you'd rather
        see a native tree running in the page, try the{" "}
        <a href="/sharedtree/checklist">live checklist</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        In Gleam, <code>Tree(List(String))</code> ties the view to its compiled
        schema. Reads give you ordinary list snapshots; edits go through a
        <code>Ref(List(String))</code> that identifies the array in the tree.
        Changing a snapshot won't change the shared document.
      </p>
      <p class="provenance">
        Fluid source is an MIT-licensed snapshot from{" "}
        <a href={fluidSource}>commit <code>{upstreamCommit.slice(0, 12)}</code></a>.
        The linked upstream package requests Fluid <code>^3.1.0</code>; that
        isn't a claim that watershed implements that entire SDK release.
        Both columns are extracted from checked-in source, not retyped for
        this page.
      </p>
      <nav aria-label="Comparison sections">
        {itemCounterRows.map(row => <a href={`#${row.id}`}>{row.id === "lifecycle" ? "Create and open" : row.id === "observe" ? "Read and subscribe" : row.id === "schema" ? "Schema" : "Edits"}</a>)}
      </nav>
    </div>

    {itemCounterRows.map(row => (
      <section class="g-block comparison-row" id={row.id} data-comparison-row={row.id} aria-labelledby={`${row.id}-title`}>
        <h2 id={`${row.id}-title`}>{row.title}</h2>
        <p>{row.explanation}</p>
        <div class="comparison-pair">
          <div class="comparison-column" data-comparison-column="fluid">
            <h3>Fluid · TypeScript</h3>
            {row.fluid.map(snippet => <SnippetBlock snippet={snippet} />)}
          </div>
          <div class="comparison-column" data-comparison-column="watershed">
            <h3>watershed · Gleam</h3>
            {row.watershed.map(snippet => <SnippetBlock snippet={snippet} />)}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}

    <section class="g-block limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
      <h2 id="limits-title">The same task isn't the same container.</h2>
      <p>
        Fluid's detached create, initialize, and attach sequence isn't a
        one-for-one match for watershed's create-with-schema, connect, and
        open-tree flow. The Gleam example uses its own schema namespace
        and the native Floodgate container layout. These apps aren't presented
        as opening each other's documents.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Gleam list is a snapshot, not a live Fluid node. The typed reference
        gives you access to the shared array, but reads and edits can fail.
        The example handles those failures through
        <code>watershed/tree/error.Error</code> rather than treating a missing
        or unreadable root as an empty list.
      </p>
      <p>
        And despite the name, this isn't a numeric counter DDS. The displayed
        number is the array's length. Two concurrent removals can target the
        same entry, so two Remove clicks don't promise a global decrement of
        two. What survives is decided by the array's merge rules.
      </p>
      <p>
        The complete example includes setup, typed reads, error handling, and
        subscription cleanup that would distract from some of these excerpts.
        It uses development-only browser token minting. Production
        authentication belongs on a backend, not in a shipped tenant secret.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="g-block run-guide" aria-labelledby="run-title">
      <h2 id="run-title">Put it in two tabs.</h2>
      <p>
        Start Floodgate with <code>just integration-up</code>. In{" "}
        <code>examples/shared_tree_item_counter_lustre</code>, run{" "}
        <code>pnpm install</code>, <code>pnpm run build</code>, then{" "}
        <code>pnpm run serve</code>. Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080</code>,
        wait for a <code>document</code> parameter, and copy the full URL into
        another tab.
      </p>
      <p>
        Insert in either tab. Remove at zero. Reload after an edit reaches the
        other tab. The{" "}
        <a href={watershedSource}>README and complete Gleam source</a>{" "}
        explain the development profile and browser gate. To run the Fluid
        version, follow the{" "}
        <a href={fluidSource}>original project's instructions</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Ecosystem />
</Sheet>

<style>
  .comparison-hero {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem) var(--content-pad);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .comparison-hero > div {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .back-link {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 20ch;
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    font-weight: 640;
    font-stretch: 122%;
    line-height: 0.99;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  h1 em {
    color: var(--overprint-deep);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .lede {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    max-width: 60ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 0.6vw + 1rem, 1.3125rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--waterline);
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }

  a:hover {
    color: var(--overprint-deep);
  }

  .source-links,
  nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-md) var(--space-xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .doc-body {
    max-width: 76rem;
  }

  .provenance {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .comparison-row {
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    scroll-margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .comparison-pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .comparison-column {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .comparison-column h3 {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .comparison-column :global(.g-file) {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .comparison-column :global(.g-code pre:focus-visible) {
    outline: 2px solid var(--overprint);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .run-guide {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .comparison-pair {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-lg);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 8.5vw, 2.7rem);
      font-stretch: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
